      "text": "A district of Asia Minor, where the cities of Iconium, Lystra, and Derbe are found (Acts 14:6). The “speech of Lycaonia” (14:11) was a dialect the people used, but they were also able to understand the Greek spoken by Paul and Barnabas.",
